Core4loop source package

Lean/Lake: 4.29.0. Main import/file: Core4loop / Core4loop.lean.
Required sibling dependency: ../Core3loop. Preserve that relative layout.
Build from this directory with the supplied dependency locks:
  lake build Core4loop
  lake build +Core4loop.Square.Rank.CombinedRank

Final proof entry points and fully qualified declarations
  Square: Core4loop/Square/Rank/CombinedRank.lean
    Core4loop.DeltaNF_square_closed
  Triangle plus leaf: Core4loop/TriangleLeaf/CorrectedFacade.lean
    Core4loop.TriangleLeaf.DeltaNF_triangleLeaf_eq_pow_X1CorrectedZ
  Diamond: Core4loop/SquareDiagonal/CorrectedFacade.lean
    Core4loop.SquareDiagonal.DeltaNF_squareDiagonal_eq_pow_X3CorrectedZ
  K4: Core4loop/CompleteGraph/CorrectedFinal.lean
    Core4loop.DeltaNF_complete_eq_pow_X4CorrectedZ

The square result needs import Core4loop.Square.Rank.CombinedRank; import
Core4loop alone does not expose that unconditional endpoint. The other three
corrected endpoints are imported by Core4loop.lean.

These are raw finite-assignment signed-sum evaluations over F2 (logical level
7: DeltaNF = 2^X). All four block sizes are positive. The three corrected
endpoints assume natural n, [NeZero n], and 2 <= n. The square theorem is
stronger in n and requires only [NeZero n].

Use X1CorrectedZ, X3CorrectedZ, and X4CorrectedZ for the respective final
results. Historical X1Z/X3Z/X4Z and PaperOld definitions remain for provenance;
they are not interchangeable with the corrected exponents. Provenance is in
TriangleLeaf/CorrectedExponent.lean, SquareDiagonal/CorrectedProvenance.lean,
and CompleteGraph/CorrectedProvenance.lean, under the Core4loop source folder.
The exact statements and their scope are in ../THEOREM_MAP.txt.

This release does not add or certify Core4 proper-support/Gamma extraction or
the manuscript contraction-to-assignment bridge. A raw endpoint is not itself
a theorem about those additional layers.

Prerequisites, pinned dependency setup, and checksum commands: ../BUILDING.txt.
No compilation was performed for this packaging revision; see ../VERIFICATION.txt.
